hey everyone welcome to yessi tv where  you can find weekly videos on minimalism  and healthy living to help you live a  simpler happier life  today i want to talk to you about  something that's a bit controversial and  it's  why i do not have social media i quit  social media about five years ago and i  do not see myself going back  so today i'm gonna share with you my six  reasons for why i quit in the first  place  and if you stick to the end you will get  my tips and tricks of things that i do  to maintain my relationships reason  number one  superficiality i had lots of  friends on social media but they felt  superficial and  fake not the individuals but the  relationships  they didn't know what my life was like  at home they didn't know that i faced  depression  and much less would they have known why  these were not the kinds of friendships  that i wanted i didn't want to have  500 friends but not have a single person  to talk to about  real life deep situations and what i was  actually going through and facing in my  life  fear of loneliness i mentioned in a  previous video  how i overcame social anxiety that i was  actually given a diagnosis  of social anxiety disorder having said  this  i was scared to talk to people but i did  want friends  that little facebook message alert  suddenly became addicting to me  i loved to see that little guy pop up  and i call it addiction  because i was happy when it was there  and sad and lonely when it wasn't  it was as if the more messages and likes  and friends i had  the more it meant people actually liked  me that maybe i wasn't a loser after all  this just made my social anxiety much  worse  i'm kind of nerdy so i have to share  just a tiny bit of an article that i was  reading  on the effects of social media and  mental health just stick with me  short one of the studies indicated that  internet use in general  significantly affects social  relationships  and participation in community life in  this research  authors found that increased time spent  online is related to a decline in  communication with family members  as well as a reduction in the user's  social circle  which may further lead to increased  feelings of depression  and loneliness and if you just search  the terms  social media and its effects on mental  health i bet you there are hundreds  of thousands of articles just like these  [Music]  validation i wanted to be  liked no pun intended i had to post just  the right picture at  just the right angle because it felt as  though the more likes i got the more it  meant people actually liked me  and for someone with very low  self-esteem it really only meant that i  was  spending hours a day scrolling through  pictures of  gorgeous people living perfect lives and  only putting myself down because  i wasn't living that way and i didn't  look the part  i didn't have the perfect lifestyle the  perfect family the perfect body the  perfect wardrobe  and for me it meant that i was  constantly feeling less than  others because i was seeking validation  from outside myself  as though others perceptions of me  mattered more  than what i perceived myself to be i  would spend  hours trying to take the perfect profile  photo  only to change it later on because it  wasn't good enough  have you ever been guilty of this one  let me know in the comments  missing out the fourth reason why i quit  social media is because i was missing  out on the world around me  five years ago on a beautiful fall  afternoon i caught myself on a  beautiful mountain top gorgeous view i  had never been there before  and i realized i had a problem when i  immediately my first thought when i was  there was  let me whip out my phone so i can take a  picture and post all about it  i didn't know how to be present in the  moment and enjoy the situation i was in  because i was constantly in this routine  of post  talk about it picture i was missing out  on amazing experiences because  my attention was focused on letting the  world know about it rather than me  enjoying it  escape one of the other reasons why i  quit social media is not only because it  was what i turned to  to face happy situations but it was also  a way to escape  negative situations in my life and this  is for several reasons  reason number one is i could avoid  stressful and negative thoughts and  memories  because it provided me with an easy  distraction reason number two  is i could avoid crucial conversations  with other people  because it was so much easier to message  them than actually speak to them face to  face  and for someone with social anxiety this  was perfect  it meant i didn't have to face my fear  of talking to people  face to face and reason number three i  could escape feelings of boredom  because it tricked me into thinking that  i was actually doing something even  though  not all too productive which leads me to  my last reason  lack of productivity i have a confession  to make  i used to follow the lives of the  kardashians and waste  hours of my time just following the  lives of reality tv stars  i don't know maybe if i watched enough  lives of millionaires i could become one  too  no the truth is we all have the same  24 hours in a day and i was done being  the consumer spending hours a day  consuming the information that other  people put out  i wanted to be more focused on how i  could be the producer  and how i could be a boss how i could  give a service to the world instead of  constantly just being a consumer once i  quit social media it  instantly increased my productivity  because it freed up hours of my day  that i could actually now invest in  myself and improving  my abilities and my knowledge base so  that i could accomplish the goals that i  had for myself  because before all that i didn't even  have goals to begin with  so between all of those things that i've  mentioned the fear of loneliness the  need for validation  the superficiality the easy escape  missing out and the lack of productivity  social media is just not for me  if you're interested in leaving social  media but you're afraid of how it might  affect your relationships  i've got three tips for you of things  that i do to kind of maintain and keep  up with your relationships  tip number one ask people for their  birthdays or any special events or  occasions or holidays that they  celebrate  and jot those down in your calendar and  make sure  that once they're there that you have it  to where it's recurring so that it will  remind you  to give them a call or to message them  on that day  preferably call them what better way to  tell someone happy birthday than to  actually give them a call  and wish them happy birthday i know for  me i have one friend that will  always call me on my birthday and even  if i don't answer she will leave a  message  and sing that song to me and it makes me  feel very special  tip number two is to actually call  someone once a week  you can do more frequently if you feel  like that you have time for it  but to actually schedule it in as  something recurring is a habit ingrained  in you is going to be  so much better at maintaining those  relationships  and i say call because this way  you can actually have a much more deeper  conversation  how many times has somebody passed you  on the street saying how  are you and you say good as they're  walking away from you  messaging can be very similar it can be  very superficial so pick up the phone  you can hear their tone of voice and  actually have a deeper conversation  lastly tip number three make sure you  contact people frequently or routinely  when you don't need something the last  thing that people want is to be that  person of  oh he's calling me because he needs me  for something  so make sure you're constantly looking  to serve others  and find out how they're doing and what  they're needing  rather than finding your needs met there  you have it guys my six reasons for why  i quit social media and why i do not  intend to go back if you like this video  please give me a thumbs up  and subscribe so that you won't miss out  on my weekly videos  i thank you so much for watching and i  hope to see you in the next one
 

